---
/**
 * /adult-drivers-ed/texas/texas-written-knowledge-test — "texas dps written test", "does adult drivers ed include
 * the written test", "texas dps written test online".
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-10-13 on the hook → answer → loop → funnel recipe (~/Claude/SEO/ADE-PAGE-RECIPE.md). The buying
 * question is whether the course covers the written test. The only wording for what it does is CLAIM
 * (ade-eligibility.ts, §521.167); what DPS still tests comes from §521.161 (process.examParts) and this page's
 * own text (vision and the driving skills test). §84.40(j): never promise a license.
 */
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import { law, process, course, CLAIM } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';

const base = '/adult-drivers-ed/texas';
const parts = process.examParts.length; // 6

// The one-breath answer: lede and meta description.
const answer = `An approved Texas adult drivers ed course ${CLAIM}. Vision and the driving test stay at DPS.`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is on the Texas written driving test?', a: `Highway signs, Texas traffic laws, bicyclists and distracted driving. Tex. Transp. Code §521.161 sets the content: your ability to identify and understand highway signs that regulate, warn or direct traffic; your knowledge of Texas traffic laws; motorists' rights and responsibilities in relation to bicyclists; and the effect of using a wireless communication device or otherwise driving distracted. Vision is tested separately, and the driving skills test is separate again.` },
  { q: 'Does adult drivers ed replace the written test?', a: `Partly. The course ${CLAIM}. Under §521.167 you are not required to take the highway sign and traffic law parts of the DPS examination once a licensed driver education instructor confirms you passed them in the course. The vision test and the driving skills test remain.` },
  { q: 'Do I still take a test if I do the course?', a: `Yes, inside the course. It ends with a two-part examination of ${course.finalExamQuestions} questions, ${course.finalExamSigns} on highway signs and ${course.finalExamLaws} on traffic laws, and you need ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part. That is the examination DPS accepts in place of its own written portions.` },
  { q: 'Is the Texas written test hard?', a: 'It covers material that is published in full. The Texas Driver Handbook covers everything on it, and so does an approved driver education course. People who fail it generally have not read either.' },
  { q: 'Can I take the written test online?', a: 'Not as a standalone DPS transaction for a first license. Either you sit the written portions at a DPS office, or you complete an approved driver education course and a licensed instructor certifies those portions for you.' },
];

const next = [
  { href: `${base}/final-exam`, title: 'The course final exam', blurb: `${course.finalExamQuestions} questions, ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part, ${course.finalExamAttempts} attempts. Its exact shape.` },
  { href: `${base}/texas-driving-test`, title: 'The driving skills test', blurb: 'The part of the DPS exam the course does not satisfy, and what to expect at it.' },
  { href: `${base}/how-to-get-a-texas-license-as-an-adult`, title: 'The whole process, step by step', blurb: 'From the course to the card in your hand, in order.' },
  { href: `${base}/cost`, title: 'What the course costs', blurb: 'One price, with the exam and the certificate in it.' },
];
---
<AdeGuide
  title={`Texas DPS Written Test: What Adult Drivers Ed Satisfies (2 of ${parts} Parts) | Road Ready Safety`}
  description={answer}
  url={`${base}/texas-written-knowledge-test`}
  eyebrow="DPS process"
  h1={`Texas DPS written test: adult drivers ed satisfies two of the six parts the law requires`}
  lede={`${answer} The statute lists six things the exam must cover, two of them are not what people expect, and the course only counts once a licensed instructor confirms you passed. All of it is below.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  dateModified="2026-10-13"
  updated="October 13, 2026"
  band={{ eyebrow: 'The written part, done at home', heading: 'The sign and traffic law portions of the knowledge exam are in the course' }}
  next={next}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.161, Examination of License Applicants', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.167, Waiver of Certain Education and Examination Requirements', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Apply for a Texas Driver License', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/apply-texas-driver-license' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What is on the Texas DPS written test?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Highway signs, Texas traffic laws, bicyclists and distracted driving, with a vision test and a
      driving test alongside. §521.161(b) lists it. The examination must include a test of the applicant&rsquo;s:
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">vision;</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">ability to identify and understand highway signs in English that regulate, warn, or direct traffic;</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">knowledge of the traffic laws of this state;</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">knowledge of motorists&rsquo; rights and responsibilities in relation to bicyclists; and</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">knowledge of the effect of using a wireless communication device, or other distraction, on safe operation of a vehicle;</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">plus a demonstration of the ability to actually drive.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Bicyclists and distracted driving surprise people. Both are named in the statute itself, and both
      are taught in the course for that reason.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Does adult drivers ed include the written test?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The course <strong>{CLAIM}</strong>, and only those portions. §521.167 sets this out:
    </p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-border pl-5 py-1 m-0">
      <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px] italic m-0">&ldquo;{law.examWaiver}&rdquo;</p>
      <cite class="text-sm text-text-muted not-italic">&mdash; Tex. Transp. Code §521.167</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Vision is still tested at the office, and the driving skills test still happens. The course
      counts only once a licensed driver education instructor determines that you passed those
      portions, which is what the examination at the end of the course is for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Can I take the Texas written test online?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Not as a standalone DPS test for a first license. The online route is an approved course, and you
      still sit an exam, the course&rsquo;s own, at home.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The course ends with a {course.finalExamQuestions}-question examination in two parts,{' '}
      {course.finalExamSigns} on highway signs and {course.finalExamLaws} on traffic laws, and you need{' '}
      {course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each. You take it at home, after{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/whats-in-the-course`}>six hours of the material</a>,
      with {course.finalExamAttempts} attempts rather than a single cold sitting at a counter.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">I&rsquo;m 25 or older. Should I take the course for the written test?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      That depends on you, because at 25 and over the course is optional. For first-time applicants over
      25, DPS calls driver education &ldquo;highly recommended.&rdquo; We set out both sides in{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/drivers-ed-over-25`}>the page for drivers 25 and over</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
